    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1339-a2">

                <pb facs="1055" n="939" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg939"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 12, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to our telegram sent you earlier in the day with reference to the
                    outcome of conferences just terminated with General Villa, and after a
                    discussion at a meeting of the Mine and Smelter Operators’ Association held here
                    this afternoon at which practically all interests were represented, it occurs to
                    say that we are particularly impressed by the peculiar ability of General Scott
                    to make friends with and to gain the confidence of such men as now dominate the
                    political affairs in Mexico. We cannot but feel that this peculiar ability of
                    General Scott might be utilized with good effect in dealing with the other
                    factional leaders in Mexico, in an effort to bring about a peaceful solution of
                    the Mexican troubles.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Mine and Smelter Operators’ Association.</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
